"AC line: 'rebar.show_ticket(<id>) ... emit exactly one rebar.CrossSessionWarning' — unreachable under this recursion for the read path"],"finding":"Instrumenting the public rebar._lib_reads.show_ticket with emit_cross_session_warning causes unbounded re-entrancy: the detector cross_session_warning_for internally calls the same public show_ticket, so show_ticket -> emit -> cross_session_warning_for -> show_ticket -> emit -> ... recurses until RecursionError, which the helper's blanket except swallows — suppressing the very warning the show_ticket acceptance criterion requires.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f08d660b085cb9fcb","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / helper body; _lib_reads.py show_ticket (:40); cross_session.py cross_session_warning_for (:36)","norm_id":"n6126573d396978cb","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Acting session B calls rebar.show_ticket(<A-held id>): expected one CrossSessionWarning, actual is deep recursion then swallowed error and zero warnings"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Point cross_session_warning_for's internal state read at the un-instrumented internal reader (rebar._reads.show_ticket) rather than the public rebar._lib_reads.show_ticket, so emitting from the public show_ticket cannot re-enter itself; alternatively add a re-entrancy guard around emit_cross_session_warning.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion covering link/unlink's id1-endpoint emission (and, at least by a parametrized test over all 13 functions, that each single-ticket function emits when acting cross-session).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope covers show_ticket, deps, transition, reopen, comment, edit_ticket, link, unlink, tag, untag, archive, set_file_impact, declare_no_file_impact","ACs only name show_ticket and comment as emitters; link's id1-endpoint rule ('pass id1') is asserted but only touched by the defect-seeded 'point at the wrong endpoint' mutation, with no positive AC"],"finding":"The scope modifies 13 single-ticket functions but the acceptance criteria only verify emission for show_ticket and comment (plus bulk-exclusion); the other 11 functions — notably link/unlink whose id1-endpoint selection is a non-trivial design choice — have no covering criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5bf0bead857e9ce8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria / Scope (single-ticket functions list)","norm_id":"n6ca37cb8ae0cb9f4","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add an AC: 'rebar.link(<A-held id1>, <id2>) as session B emits exactly one CrossSessionWarning naming holder A of id1, and NOT id2's holder (parametrized coverage asserting every single-ticket function in scop