it__.py __all__ as re-exports."],"finding":"The plan's inventory of single-ticket public library functions to cover omits `check_ac` and `clarity_check`, even though the plan asserts parity with the CLI surface it names ('matching the CLI (S3)'). The CLI's authoritative warn set `_CROSS_SESSION_WARN_COMMANDS` (src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py:22-39) includes `check-ac` and `clarity-check`; both map to single-ticket library functions taking `ticket_id` that are re-exported as `rebar.check_ac` / `rebar.clarity_check` (src/rebar/_lib_gates.py:61,35; src/rebar/__init__.py __all__). Neither appears in the plan's Approach coverage list or Scope, so both library reads would silently not emit CrossSessionWarning, breaking the claimed CLI parity.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f54e6411ed5be930c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'The single-ticket public functions to cover, at their actual definition sites'; and Scope — src/rebar/_lib_gates.py bullet","norm_id":"n6233370b38dfaa83","priority":0.8889,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["src/rebar/_lib_gates.py:check_ac — a call site the plan never patches; `rebar.check_ac(<A-held id>)` acting as session B emits no CrossSessionWarning while the CLI's `check-ac` does, so library/CLI parity the plan claims is broken.","src/rebar/_lib_gates.py:clarity_check — same: `rebar.clarity_check(<A-held id>)` emits no warning though the CLI `clarity-check` is in _CROSS_SESSION_WARN_COMMANDS.","The Scope's _lib_gates.py bullet lists only set_file_impact and declare_no_file_impact, so the two read gates go unpatched and are not exercised by any AC/test — a silent under-delivery of the parity goal."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Extend the _lib_gates.py coverage/Scope to call `emit_cross_session_warning(ticket_id, repo_root=repo_root)` in `check_ac` (:61) and `clarity_check` (:35) as well, matching the CLI's check-ac/clarity-check entries; leave quality_check and set_verify_commands o